      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function",
      "problem": "What is the value of $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-4) \\\\ 5t \\\\ 1-2t\\end{aligned}]$ at $t=5?$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute $t=5$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(5) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5-4) \\\\ 5(5) \\\\ 1-2(5)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\ {5}^{2} \\\\ 1-10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 25 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the value of $f(t)$ at $t=5$ is the vector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 25 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].$",
